From: OpenWrt Team <openwrt@openwrt.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 001] Add -Dmodulesdir meson option

The pkcs11-provider meson build derives the OpenSSL modules install path
from pkg-config's 'modulesdir' variable.  When cross-compiling, the host
pkg-config returns the host system path instead of the sysroot path, which
causes the .so to be installed into the wrong directory (or triggers a
DESTDIR double-nesting bug).

Add an explicit -Dmodulesdir= meson option so the OpenWrt Makefile can
pass the correct staging/target directory directly, bypassing pkg-config.
---
 meson.build       | 7 ++++++-
 meson_options.txt | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -48,7 +48,12 @@ conf.set('PACKAGE_MAJOR', major_version)
 conf.set('PACKAGE_MINOR', minor_version)
 
 libcrypto = dependency('libcrypto', version: '>= 3.0.7')
-provider_path = libcrypto.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'modulesdir')
+modulesdir_opt = get_option('modulesdir')
+if modulesdir_opt == ''
+  provider_path = libcrypto.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'modulesdir')
+else
+  provider_path = modulesdir_opt
+endif
 libssl = dependency('libssl', version: '>= 3.0.7')

